   The reaction between sulphur and oxygen to form SO₂ is:
   \[
   \text{S} + \frac{3}{2} \text{O} = \text{SO}_2
   \]
   The molar weight of S is 16 g/mol, and the molar weight of O is 16 g/mol. The molar weight of SO₂ is 16 (for S) + 16 (for O) + 16 (for O) = 48 g/mol.

