\[ \text{Area of one paving stone} = 2.5 \, \text{m} \times w \]

Since 165 paving stones cover the entire courtyard, the total area covered by the paving stones is:
\[ 165 \times (2.5 \, \text{m} \times w) = 825 \, \text{m}^2 \]

Now we can set up the equation:
\[ 165 \times (2.5 \, \text{m} \times w) = 825 \, \text{m}^2 \]

Solving for \( w \):
\[ 165 \times 2.5 \, \text{m} \times w = 825 \, \text{m}^2 \]
\[ 412.5 \, \text{m} \times w = 825 \, \text{m}^2 \]
\[ w = \frac{825 \, \text{m}^2}{412.5 \, \text{m}} \]
