\[
t = \frac{3}{\sqrt{1 - (0.6c)^2/c^2}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{1 - 0.36}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{0.6}} \approx 3.33 \text{ years}
\]

Since the clock in the cockpit shows 3 years when the ship returns to Earth, the time on the Earth's clock is approximately 3.33 hours.

