\]
where \(A\) and \(B\) are constants. The derivative of \(H(t)\) is:
\[
\dot{H}(t) = A w \cos(wt) + B w \cos(wt).
\]
The second derivative of \(H(t)\) is:
\[
\ddot{H}(t) = -A w^2 \sin(wt) - B w^2 \sin(wt).
\]
