- \( x \) is the displacement of the oscillator from its equilibrium position
- \( \dot{x} \) is the velocity of the oscillator (\( \dot{x} = \dot{x} \))
- \( \ddot{x} \) is the acceleration of the oscillator (\( \ddot{x} = \ddot{x} \))
- \( m \) is the mass of the oscillator
- \( m_0 \) is the mass of the oscillator
- \( \frac{m}{m_0} \) is the damping coefficient

The equation of motion for an unddelayed harmonic oscillator with damping is:

\[
\ddot{x} + \frac{k}{m} \dot{x} + \frac{k}{m} x = 0
\]

where:
- \( x \) is the displacement of the oscillator from its equilibrium position
- \( \dot{x} \) is the velocity of the oscillator (\( \dot{x} = \dot{x} \))
- \( \ddot{x} \) is the acceleration of the oscillator (\( \ddot{x} = \ddot{x} \))
- \( m \) is the mass of the oscillator
- \( k \) is the spring constant (or the constant related to the damping system)

